file C:\NEWSLTR\ISSUE14.DOC
	icon: res://win95/office/icons/word_document_32.png
	modified: Thursday, May 30, 1996 10:47:31 PM
	contents:
		{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0\froman Times New Roman;}}\f0\fs20
		\qc\b\fs36 ELM PARK NEWS\b0\fs20\par
		\qc\i Friends of Elm Park. Issue 14, June 1996.\i0\par
		\ql\par
		\b\fs24 The vote is June 12\b0\fs20\par
		The city council votes on June 12 on paving Elm Park for a 300-car parking lot. Come to the meeting at 7 pm in the council chamber. Bring a neighbour. Bring a chair; they never have enough.\par
		\par
		\b\fs24 437 and counting\b0\fs20\par
		Sign the petition at the library or at CompuFun's counter. Every name counts on June 12.\par
		\par
		\b\fs24 A parking lot is not a park\b0\fs20\par
		Elm Park has an old elm, a pond with three ducks, and the only shade on Main Street. A parking lot has 300 cars and no shade. The council says the town needs the parking. We say the town needs somewhere to park itself.\par
		\par
		\b\fs24 Classifieds\b0\fs20\par
		FOR SALE: Bake sale leftovers. Marge has them. Ask nicely.\par
		WANTED: Floppy disks labelled "update" by hand, 13 disks in a set. Will pay $5 a set. Ask Bob.\par
		\par
		\i The newsletter doesn't write itself. Write to Bob: bob@aol.com\i0\par
		}

